_site/
.jekyll-cache/
.jekyll-metadata
Gemfile.lock
vendor/
# The prose-review documents ARE ignored, as of 2026-08-26, at the owner's
# request -- fifteen rounds had accumulated in the working tree. This reverses
# the policy the previous comment here argued for, and the argument was not
# wrong: an edited .odt is the owner's own hand and cannot be rebuilt from
# anything else. What makes ignoring them safe is that nothing is lost -- every
# round up to 2026-08-31 stays in git history, and the edits themselves were
# read back into the site before the files were removed.
#
# A round's document is generated to /tmp by tools/make_review_doc.py and now
# stays there. Copy one in only if the owner asks for it, and expect it to be
# untracked. What keeps these out of the *built site* is the `exclude` list in
# _config.yml, a different mechanism; this file was briefly doing that job too
# (2ed180f) and should not have been.
*.odt
.~lock*

# Scratch directory used by tools/preview.sh while a build is in progress.
.preview-build/

# Built by tools/deploy_review.sh. Kept out of _site so a review build --
# different url, robots.txt Disallow -- can never be published by mistake.
_review_site/

# Untracked on 2026-09-03, ahead of making the repository public. All three
# stay on disk and keep working; what changes is that they are no longer
# published with the source.
#
#   _data/review_notes.yml        the owner's open questions, written for him
#                                 rather than for a reader. tools/make_review_doc.py
#                                 reads it from disk and does not care that it is
#                                 untracked.
#   docs/NAMESPACE_AND_REDIRECTS.md  domain and repository decisions, including
#                                 the glow-erc.org non-renewal, a path into the
#                                 owner's Overleaf project, and a conversation
#                                 with a collaborator that has not happened yet.
#   glow-site-text_MZ.html        the whole site's text in one file, already
#                                 excluded from the build by `exclude` in
#                                 _config.yml. Tracking it published a second
#                                 copy of every page with none of the review.
#
# Untracking does NOT remove them from git history. See the note at the end of
# this file.
_data/review_notes.yml
docs/NAMESPACE_AND_REDIRECTS.md
glow-site-text_MZ.html
